<!DOCTYPE html>
@*
    The theme of the page, which the server decides for every page that it answers with: the
    theme of the account of a user, and the theme that the device of a visitor saved (FR-THM-3).
    It is said here, on the first element and ahead of the stylesheets, so the page is in its
    theme before anything of it is painted, and no script has a part in it (FR-THM-4). A page
    that looks as the device is set says nothing, and the stylesheet follows the device
    (FR-THM-2). See docs/themes.md.

    Beside it the page says "reduced" when its user chose that less of the pages moves
    (FR-ANI-4), and nothing otherwise: the stylesheet then gives what moves to a device that
    does not ask for reduced motion. See docs/motion.md.
*@
<html lang="@Screens.Language" data-theme="@PageTheme.AttributeOf(Theme)" data-motion="@PageMotion.AttributeOf(Motion)">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    @* Which of light and dark the page may be, for what the browser paints before the stylesheets are there. *@
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="@PageTheme.ColorSchemeOf(Theme)" />
    <base href="/" />
    <ResourcePreloader />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["Ecnanib.styles.css"]" />
    @* The one script that is written into the page. A browser runs it only with the nonce of this answer. *@
    <ImportMap nonce="@Nonce" />
    <HeadOutlet />
</head>

<body>
    @*
        The times of the page, which every page and every part of one is handed: each time is
        written in the time zone of the page (NFR-USA-3). See docs/times.md.
    *@
    <CascadingValue Value="@Times" IsFixed="true">
        <Routes />
    </CascadingValue>
    <ReconnectModal />
    @* What a page of a user says shortly before its session ends, and nothing for a visitor (NFR-USA-1). *@
    <SessionNotice />
    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
    @*
        The first of the three scripts of the application itself, for what moves and a stylesheet
        cannot do alone (FR-ANI-2 to FR-ANI-6). It is a file of this site, which the policy of
        the answer lets a browser run, and it starts once the page is read. A page works without
        it. See docs/motion.md.
    *@
    <script type="module" src="@Assets["motion.js"]"></script>
    @*
        The second, for the notice before a session ends (NFR-USA-1): it waits, asks the server
        how long is left, and shows the dialog that SessionNotice wrote. A page works without it
        too, and its session then ends as it always did. See docs/accounts.md.
    *@
    <script type="module" src="@Assets["session.js"]"></script>
    @*
        The third, for the time zone of the device (NFR-USA-3): it writes what the browser says
        its time zone is into the field of a form that asks for it, as the form of the sign-in
        does. It asks the server nothing and keeps nothing: the server writes every time. A page
        works without it too, and its times are then in UTC. See docs/times.md.
    *@
    <script type="module" src="@Assets["times.js"]"></script>
</body>

</html>

@using Ecnanib.Accounts
@using Ecnanib.Platform.Security
@using Ecnanib.WebUi.Animation
@using Ecnanib.WebUi.Themes

@code {
    [CascadingParameter]
    private HttpContext? HttpContext { get; set; }

    private string? Nonce => HttpContext is null ? null : BrowserDefenses.NonceOf(HttpContext);

    /// <summary>The theme that the page is written in.</summary>
    private Theme Theme => HttpContext is null ? Theme.System : PageTheme.Of(HttpContext);

    /// <summary>How much of the page moves.</summary>
    private Motion Motion => HttpContext is null ? Motion.System : PageMotion.Of(HttpContext);

    /// <summary>The times that the page writes a time in: those of the time zone of its request.</summary>
    private PageTimes Times => HttpContext is null ? PageTimes.Utc : PageTimes.Of(HttpContext);
}
